00:57:10,702 --> 00:57:23,378
A 3.2 degree of difficulty to get her five dives up and running.

493
00:57:23,398 --> 00:57:26,182
Again, anything around mid-70s is a solid start.

494
00:57:27,724 --> 00:57:33,233
Chinese divers will be looking for the mid-80s, but anything mid-70s, it's just about right.

495
00:57:33,273 --> 00:57:34,894
Toes nicely pointed.

496
00:57:35,715 --> 00:57:36,556
Entry good.

497
00:57:38,208 --> 00:57:40,070
And a 75.2 score.

498
00:57:40,672 --> 00:57:41,612
Two eights and a 7.5.

499
00:57:42,373 --> 00:57:45,858
The judges scores the count multiplied by the degree of difficulty.

500
00:57:51,025 --> 00:57:52,108
First of the two Canadians.

501
00:57:52,148 --> 00:57:53,710
This is Rosalind Filion.

502
00:57:53,730 --> 00:57:55,552
Tiny diver.

503
00:57:57,775 --> 00:57:58,516
Bundle of energy.

504
00:57:59,599 --> 00:58:01,161
Forward three and a half somersault.

505
00:58:18,657 --> 00:58:19,878
Nice, confident approach.

506
00:58:22,202 --> 00:58:23,184
And the coaches are happy.

507
00:58:23,224 --> 00:58:25,949
They think she's nailed it.

508
00:58:25,989 --> 00:58:34,422
A bronze at the 2012 Summer Olympics in the Synchro event.

509
00:58:45,050 --> 00:58:46,733
Spotting the entry.

510
00:58:47,213 --> 00:58:49,657
She's picked up 63 points.

511
00:58:50,297 --> 00:58:53,722
It did take a long time to set herself before getting into that tuck.

512
00:59:04,119 --> 00:59:07,483
And the entry.

513
00:59:07,503 --> 00:59:13,773
Not exactly perpendicular, so Megan has 64 for 137.5.

514
00:59:20,976 --> 00:59:28,206
The danger is she might drop from second to fifth, such as the tightness of competition in this women's final.

515
00:59:29,389 --> 00:59:31,711
This is the clear leader from the first round.

516
00:59:32,813 --> 00:59:34,896
An inward three and a half somersault in tuck.

517
00:59:46,351 --> 00:59:47,152
Lovely spring.

518
00:59:48,989 --> 00:59:51,030
Yeah, just that little bit of extra height.

519
00:59:51,110 --> 01:00:01,922
Tight somersaults.

520
01:00:01,942 --> 01:00:02,681
Nice tight tuck.

521
01:00:02,822 --> 01:00:08,128
Always seems to have so much time and barely a ripple on entry into the pool.

522
01:00:14,833 --> 01:00:17,697
That's a 78.4.

523
01:00:18,891 --> 01:00:28,309
And top ranked again in 8.5.

524
01:00:28,329 --> 01:00:29,552
It was a nine.

525
01:00:30,132 --> 01:00:32,016
Marked by one of the judges as the highest.

526
01:00:32,336 --> 01:00:35,784
And the 7.5 chalked off.

527
01:00:35,804 --> 01:00:37,085
So after two rounds.

528
01:00:37,909 --> 01:00:44,099
Xu Xia leads 14.8 points clear of Pandalela Rinong, who is just 0.5 clear of Tonya Couch.

529
01:00:45,039 --> 01:00:46,181
That's a good battle.

530
01:00:46,501 --> 01:00:51,849
Any one of second to sixth could be in the podium at the end of five rounds.

531
01:00:51,929 --> 01:00:53,251
But good start from Pandalela.

532
01:00:53,873 --> 01:01:00,001
Tonya, very competitive but outstanding from the Chinese athlete Liu Xu Xia.

533
01:01:06,918 --> 01:01:18,077
We are at the WaterCube, the venue for the Diving World Series 2014, the first competition of the season here in Beijing.

534
01:01:20,300 --> 01:01:25,208
It's the eighth season of the FINA Diving World Series, sponsored this year by NVC Lighting.

535
01:01:29,856 --> 01:01:31,440
Mexican fans everywhere.

536
01:01:36,128 --> 01:01:37,130
Alejandro Roscoe.

537
01:01:40,197 --> 01:01:48,737
Great experience for the 16 year old.

538
01:02:15,952 --> 01:02:20,498
A 3.2 degree of difficulty for that inward three and a half somersault.

539
01:02:24,983 --> 01:02:30,630
The youngest ever athlete to represent Mexico at the 2012 Olympics.

540
01:02:37,498 --> 01:02:39,201
It's a very solid dive.

541
01:02:41,163 --> 01:02:45,268
Recognized by the judges little peek at the scoreboard 72.

542
01:02:46,463 --> 01:02:49,327
37.5, the scores the count from the judges.

543
01:02:51,733 --> 01:02:55,559
Little nod of approval from her coaches on the poolside.

544
01:02:55,599 --> 01:03:00,088
Tonya Couch from Plymouth.

545
01:03:02,873 --> 01:03:04,336
Forward three and a half somersault.

546
01:03:17,210 --> 01:03:18,552
Good confidence approach.

547
01:03:18,632 --> 01:03:21,456
Nice spring into the dive.

548
01:03:24,440 --> 01:03:26,483
Just gets that little bit of extra air.

549
01:03:28,005 --> 01:03:32,992
What's the execution like in the air?

550
01:03:43,847 --> 01:03:46,811
The marking is a 67.5.

551
01:03:49,693 --> 01:03:51,996
She doesn't bring nods of approval from Tonya.

552
01:03:52,016 --> 01:03:53,577
I think she thought she was a little bit better than that.

553
01:03:53,597 --> 01:03:54,458
Goes to the coaches.

554
01:04:04,210 --> 01:04:13,219
Filion currently ranked sixth, but a good dive here, which is possibly a little bit less than I think the coaches reckon she deserved.

555
01:04:13,760 --> 01:04:15,583
Three sevens the scores that count.

556
01:04:17,757 --> 01:04:19,661
Instant feedback from all the coaches.

557
01:04:20,481 --> 01:04:22,005
Alright, Malaysia's Pandalela Rinong.

558
01:04:24,048 --> 01:04:27,876
Bronze medalist at the 2012 Olympics in this competition.

559
01:04:31,061 --> 01:04:33,326
Forward three and a half somersault in the pike position.

560
01:04:33,847 --> 01:04:36,271
The agree of difficulty 3.0.

561
01:04:50,527 --> 01:04:53,630
Again, a lovely clean entry into the water from Pandalela.

562
01:04:59,978 --> 01:05:03,981
She's still only 21 years of age, comes from East Malaysia, Sarawak.

563
01:05:04,001 --> 01:05:07,766
There's much of her training up here in Beijing.

564
01:05:15,213 --> 01:05:19,978
She's picked up a 76.5 opening round score.

565
01:05:27,282 --> 01:05:32,411
That's a very solid start from Pandalela.

566
01:05:32,431 --> 01:05:34,715
Megan Benfaito, she's up next.

567
01:05:34,755 --> 01:05:39,364
The first of her five dives will be a forward three and a half somersault.

568
01:05:40,867 --> 01:05:42,530
Dive 107B as they call it.

569
01:05:43,211 --> 01:05:46,117
Same as we've just seen from Pandalela.

570
01:06:01,454 --> 01:06:04,639
25 year old who hails from Montreal in Canada.

571
01:06:06,302 --> 01:06:09,827
Again, there's good reaction from her coaches.

572
01:06:13,233 --> 01:06:15,396
She won her qualifying group earlier on this morning.

573
01:06:16,699 --> 01:06:18,021
It is always good for confidence.

574
01:06:21,306 --> 01:06:22,327
Nice tight pike.

575
01:06:24,030 --> 01:06:25,032
Spots the entry.

576
01:06:28,132 --> 01:06:29,876
Toes nice and close together.

577
01:06:29,896 --> 01:06:33,666
73.5 and 8.5 and two eights.

578
01:06:35,150 --> 01:06:36,112
The scores, the counting.

579
01:06:37,376 --> 01:06:40,163
Eight, the lowest any of the seven judges awarded at.

580
01:06:40,282 --> 01:06:43,610
Now then, the favorite, Lujica.

581
01:06:56,315 --> 01:06:59,818
The dive of choice, the forward three and a half somersault in Pike.

582
01:07:10,650 --> 01:07:11,670
Rapturous applause.

583
01:07:13,432 --> 01:07:17,076
She's rather overshadowed by Chen Ruolin is Lihui Xia.

584
01:07:18,677 --> 01:07:22,342
She won one of these tournaments in last year's World Series event.

585
01:07:23,222 --> 01:07:25,545
She's got off to a cracking start here.

586
01:07:26,318 --> 01:07:27,679
Nice tight pike.

587
01:07:29,001 --> 01:07:29,963
Confident approach.

588
01:07:32,806 --> 01:07:33,568
Straight legs.

589
01:07:35,670 --> 01:07:38,934
Out early into the dive and a perfect entry.

590
01:07:38,954 --> 01:07:45,342
82.5 is the unofficial scoring card.

591
01:07:45,362 --> 01:07:51,731
The official confirmation comes now indeed 82.5 and 9.5 and two nines.

592
01:07:53,494 --> 01:07:56,257
Anything 9.5 is perceived to be excellent.

593
01:07:57,367 --> 01:08:00,012
And that's a first round lead as expected for you.

594
01:08:00,032 --> 01:08:00,512
He's here.

595
01:08:01,394 --> 01:08:03,498
And the leather inong from Malaysia.

596
01:08:04,579 --> 01:08:08,666
Currently in second place, 1.3 points ahead of Britain's Tonya couch.

597
01:08:09,768 --> 01:08:11,672
With Megan Bonifeto a further 1.7.

598
01:08:13,315 --> 01:08:14,737
Down in fourth place.

599
01:08:14,918 --> 01:08:15,798
Good start.

600
01:08:28,908 --> 01:08:30,791
Back to Alejandro Orozco.

601
01:08:34,716 --> 01:08:36,399
She'll start this time with an arm stand.

602
01:08:38,342 --> 01:08:42,109
And then we'll release into a back double somersault.

603
01:08:43,511 --> 01:08:45,274
Really have difficulty 3.2.

604
01:08:50,762 --> 01:08:53,768
Looking for the approach, you're looking for how solid the arm stand is.

605
01:09:24,697 --> 01:09:28,310
Athletic agility and strength required at the top of the dive.

